[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following fungi is known for causing nosocomial outbreaks, is often resistant to standard antifungal agents, and may necessitate enhanced infection control measures in healthcare settings?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Scedosporium prolificans   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Fonsecaea pedrosoi   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Alternaria infectoria   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Wallemia sebi   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Exophiala werneckii   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Plectophomella   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Phialophora richardsiae
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
