[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Advances in ecological research and conservation biology increasingly rely on sophisticated statistical tools and concepts, including Bayesian model comparison, measures of biodiversity, and software platforms for statistical modeling. Understanding how these elements interconnect is essential for modern scientific investigation in evolutionary and ecological studies.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following best characterizes the purpose of phylogenetic diversity in conservation biology?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) To maximize the number of individuals in an ecosystem regardless of species   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) To ensure the protection of species based solely on their abundance   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) To prioritize conservation efforts based on the evolutionary relationships among species   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) To implement probabilistic programming languages for ecological data analysis   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) To compare Bayesian models using Bayes factors   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) To increase genetic variation within a single species   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) To estimate ecosystem biomass using hierarchical statistical models
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
