[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Ammonia-oxidizing bacteria (AOB) and archaea play crucial roles in the global nitrogen cycle, with diverse metabolic pathways and adaptations enabling them to thrive in various environments. Advances in genomics and biochemistry have illuminated key enzymes and regulatory mechanisms underlying ammonia oxidation and stress adaptation in these microorganisms.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which enzyme subunit in Nitrosomonas europaea has been specifically identified as functioning in stress response rather than being essential for ammonia oxidation itself?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) AmoA   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) AmoB   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) AmoC3   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Nitrite reductase (NirK)   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Nitric oxide reductase (NorB)   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Cytochrome P460   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Cytochrome c'-beta
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. 
