[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m If the bacterium is using nitrite for electron transfer, maybe it's using it as an alternative for oxygen. But wait, in anaerobic conditions, even with nitrite, the primary ATP production would still depend on SLP. So perhaps the presence of nitrite doesn't mean the bacterium is resorting to OP, because OP isn't possible without oxygen.
