[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Option 3 suggests EtrA is the most highly expressed and induces both regulators under aerobic conditions, which seems conflicting because EtrA is supposed to be active under anaerobic conditions. Wait, is EtrA active under aerobic or anaerobic conditions? I think EtrA is involved in the switch to anaerobic metabolism, so it might be expressed when oxygen is low. So if EtrA is most highly expressed under anaerobic conditions, then under aerobic conditions, it's low. So option 3 might not be correct.
