[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m The soxRS regulon in Escherichia coli is a critical genetic system that enables the bacterium to sense and respond to oxidative and nitrosative stresses within host environments, such as those encountered during phagocytosis by activated macrophages. Understanding the mechanisms that trigger soxRS activation is essential for appreciating bacterial survival strategies under immune attack.
