[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Alternatively, maybe nitrite stress leads to the production of hydrogen peroxide, which can oxidize Fe(II) to Fe(III). This would decrease Fe(II) levels, leading to Fur activation. But again, that would cause repression, not derepression.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Wait, I'm getting confused. Let me try to approach this differently.
