[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Now, thinking about what I've read about oregano essential oil. I remember a study where thymol and carvacrol were found to inhibit the NF-κB pathway by interfering with the degradation of IκB, thus preventing NF-κB nuclear translocation. Additionally, they might influence the MAPK pathway by affecting the phosphorylation of ERK, a key part of the MAPK cascade. So, both thymol and carvacrol could be involved in modulating these pathways.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
