[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Dematiaceous (darkly pigmented) fungi are increasingly recognized as opportunistic pathogens, particularly affecting immunocompromised individuals. Some of these organisms are notable for causing rare but severe infections that can be difficult to treat.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which fungal species is most strongly associated with causing a cerebral abscess in immunocompromised patients and is known to respond to voriconazole therapy?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Curvularia lunata   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Scytalidium dimidiatum   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Cladophialophora bantiana   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Alternaria alternata   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Exserohilum rostratum   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Phialophora verrucosa   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Scedosporium prolificans
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
