[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m So in lapD mutants, when phosphate is low, they accumulate LapA inside. In wild-type, maybe under low phosphate, LapA is either on the surface or released. So if LapD is involved in releasing or transporting LapA out of the cell, the mutant can't do that, so it stays inside, especially when phosphate is scarce.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
