[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Dematiaceous fungi are melanized molds increasingly recognized as causes of severe infections in both immunocompetent and immunocompromised individuals. Their clinical manifestations range from superficial skin involvement to life-threatening central nervous system disease and are often challenging to treat due to drug resistance and variable therapeutic responses.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which fungal species is most commonly associated with brain abscesses and severe central nervous system infections in humans, particularly among dematiaceous fungi?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Scedosporium aurantiacum   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Alternaria alternata   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Exophiala jeanselmei   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Cladophialophora bantiana   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Myceliophthora thermophila   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Curvularia lunata   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Rhinocladiella atrovirens
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
