[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Lactic acid bacteria (LAB) are evaluated for their potential as probiotics in poultry, particularly for their ability to adhere to intestinal cells, aggregate, co-aggregate with pathogens, and inhibit harmful bacteria. Understanding the strain-specific nature of these properties is essential for selecting effective probiotic candidates.
