[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which statement most accurately reflects the relationship between LAB strains and their co-aggregation and antagonistic activities against various poultry pathogens?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) All LAB strains exhibit identical co-aggregation percentages with every pathogen tested.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) LAB strains I5 and I13 show no significant difference in auto-aggregation compared to other LAB strains.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) The co-aggregation ability of LAB strains is both strain- and pathogen-dependent, with notable variation in effectiveness against different pathogens.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) LAB strain c3 exhibits superior adhesion to epithelial cells compared to all pathogens after 90 minutes.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) The antagonistic activity of all LAB strains results in inhibition zones consistently less than 10 mm for all pathogens.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Co-aggregation with pathogens does not contribute to the removal of harmful bacteria from the gastrointestinal tract.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) All LAB strains show insignificant differences in their ability to inhibit E. coli O157:H7.
