[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) The antagonistic activity of all LAB strains results in inhibition zones consistently less than 10 mm for all pathogens.  
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Inhibition zones are measured in disk diffusion tests. If all strains have zones less than 10 mm, it might mean they are not effective against all pathogens. But it's possible that some strains might have better activity, so this statement may not always hold true. It could be false if there are some LAB strains with larger zones.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Co-aggregation with pathogens does not contribute to the removal of harmful bacteria from the gastrointestinal tract.  
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m This seems incorrect. Co-aggregation would help in the removal of harmful bacteria by physically taking them out or preventing their adherence. So this statement is probably false.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
