[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Necrotic enteritis (NE) in poultry, primarily caused by Clostridium perfringens, poses significant health and economic challenges to the poultry industry. Growing concerns over antibiotic resistance have driven research into alternative methods for controlling this disease.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following strategies specifically utilizes engineered fusion proteins that combine phage-derived endolysins with cell wall binding domains to enhance specificity and stability for controlling C. perfringens in poultry?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Probiotic administration   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Bacteriocin supplementation   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Live attenuated vaccination   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Yeast extract dietary intervention   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Engineered antimicrobial protein application   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Competitive exclusion cultures   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) In-feed antibiotic usage
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. Do not use markdown in the reasoning.
