[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Necrotic enteritis is a major disease affecting broiler chickens and poses significant challenges to the global poultry industry, especially following the restriction of antibiotic growth promoters. Understanding the causative agent and the mechanisms by which it induces disease is essential for developing effective control strategies.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which toxin produced by Clostridium perfringens is now recognized as essential for inducing necrotic enteritis in broiler chickens, shifting the previous focus from another toxin?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Beta toxin   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Epsilon toxin   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Alpha toxin   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) NetB toxin   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Theta toxin   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Iota toxin   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Perfrin
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
