[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Wait, another thought: when you prepare DNA standards from cloned 16S rRNA genes (option5), that would ensure that the standards are pure and don't have any primer-dimers because they're cloned. But that's about standardization, not about ensuring that your qPCR reactions don't produce non-specific signals.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
