[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following statements best characterizes the current understanding of Akkermansia muciniphila's impact on cancer immunotherapy and other disease contexts?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) It universally enhances the effectiveness of all types of cancer immunotherapy, regardless of gut microbiota composition.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Its outer membrane protein Amuc_1100 directly attacks tumor cells, leading to improved cancer outcomes.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) High levels are always beneficial for neurodegenerative diseases such as Parkinson's disease and multiple sclerosis.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Clinical use as a therapeutic adjuvant requires further human studies despite promising animal model results.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Its immunomodulatory effects are independent of interactions with other microbes in the gut.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) The presence of A. muciniphila invariably leads to reduced inflammation in every disease context.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Its benefits are solely due to metabolic regulation without involvement in immune response.
