[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Genetic tools such as reporter plasmids are essential for studying gene regulation in bacteria, especially when transferring systems between different species. Modifications to reporter systems may be necessary to ensure accurate measurement of promoter activity in non-model organisms.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which methodological change was critical for enabling accurate assessment of S. oneidensis promoter activity using a lacZ-based reporter in S. oneidensis MR-1?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Retaining the original E. coli P_lac promoter upstream of lacZ   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Inserting the lacZa gene fragment into the reporter plasmid   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Fusing native S. oneidensis promoters directly to a full-length lacZ gene   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Utilizing only suicide vectors for homologous recombination without reporter assays   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Co-expressing E. coli-specific regulatory proteins in S. oneidensis   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Introducing antibiotic resistance cassettes within the promoter region   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Deleting the entire lacZ gene from the plasmid backbone
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m The correct methodological change was option 3: Fusing native S. oneidensis promoters directly to a full-length lacZ gene.
