[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m The gut microbiome consists of trillions of microorganisms in the human digestive tract, influencing metabolic health and the risk of developing various chronic diseases. Advances in metagenomics and bioinformatics tools have enabled deeper investigation into microbial functions and host-microbe interactions.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which resource is primarily used as a reference for metabolic pathways to aid in the annotation and interpretation of microbiome metagenomic data?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) MetaCyc   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) MOCAT2   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) MG-RAST   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) MEGAN   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) TMAO   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Insulin   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Dysbiosis
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
