[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m In Pseudomonas fluorescens, the switch between motile and sessile lifestyles is tightly regulated by environmental signals and intracellular second messengers. The RapA-LapD-LapG pathway is a key signaling circuit that controls the localization and release of the adhesin protein LapA in response to phosphate availability.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which scenario most clearly demonstrates LapG's essential role in cell-surface LapA turnover during phosphate limitation?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Wild-type cells show reduced surface LapA and increased LapA in the supernatant under low phosphate.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) rapA mutants fail to alter LapA secretion or localization in response to phosphate levels.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) lapG mutants hyper-accumulate LapA on the cell surface and do not release LapA into the supernatant under any condition.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) lapD mutants have high supernatant LapA and low surface LapA, regardless of phosphate conditions.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) rapA mutants exhibit lower cell surface LapA than wild-type, but no change with phosphate levels.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Wild-type cells accumulate intracellular LapA during phosphate starvation.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) lapD mutants accumulate intracellular LapA only under low phosphate.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So, if the correct answer is option 3, then I will write \boxed{3}.
