[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Treatment of infections caused by resistant dematiaceous (melanized) fungi relies on effective antifungal strategies, including drug combinations that exploit different mechanisms of action. Understanding both in vitro and in vivo efficacy, as well as the pharmacologic limitations of available agents, is crucial in managing these challenging infections.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following statements accurately reflects findings regarding antifungal therapy for resistant dematiaceous fungal infections, particularly those involving Scedosporium prolificans?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Terbinafine is recommended for systemic infections due to its proven in vivo efficacy.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Antagonism is frequently observed when combining azoles and echinocandins against Scedosporium prolificans.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Triple-drug antifungal combinations provide marked survival benefits over dual combinations in animal models.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Posaconazole demonstrates superior efficacy compared to amphotericin B and itraconazole in central nervous system infections.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Ketoconazole consistently outperforms 5-fluorocytosine in animal studies involving dematiaceous fungi.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) The use of colony-stimulating factors always enhances antifungal efficacy in vivo.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Synergy between voriconazole and terbinafine is only observed in studies with animal models.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m The correct answer is \boxed{3}.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m </think>
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m The correct statement regarding antifungal therapy for resistant dematiaceous fungal infections is:
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Triple-drug antifungal combinations provide marked survival benefits over dual combinations in animal models.
