[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Mutation in LapA positions 108 and 109 to arginines. If these are in the cleavage region, changing them might make LapA resistant to cleavage. So that would also prevent LapG from releasing LapA.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Deletion of c-di-GMP enzymes: c-di-GMP is involved in biofilm formation. If you delete these, biofilms might be reduced, but the question is specifically about LapG and LapA interaction. Not sure if directly relevant.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Overexpression of LapA: More LapA on the surface, which would increase adhesion, but how does that interact with LapG? If LapG is still present, it might cleave more. Maybe not directly preventing release.
