[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Advances in biomaterials have led to the development of implant surface modifications that simultaneously enhance antibacterial activity, promote bone integration, and maintain compatibility with human tissue. These innovations leverage a variety of coatings, nanostructures, and bioactive agents to address challenges such as infection and poor osteointegration in orthopedic and dental implants.
