[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following strategies directly combines both targeted antimicrobial activity and specific titanium-binding capability to inhibit biofilm formation on titanium implants?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Hydrophobic polycationic polymer coatings   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Plant-synthesized metallic nanoparticles   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Totarol-based natural antibacterial coatings   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Rhamnolipid biosurfactant coatings   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Engineered chimeric peptides with antimicrobial and titanium-binding functions   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Bismuth-doped calcium phosphate cement   
