[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m The composition and stability of the human microbiome, particularly in the gut, play a crucial role in resisting pathogenic infections and maintaining health. Disruptions to the microbiome, whether by antibiotics, nanomaterials, or other interventions, can have significant consequences for disease susceptibility and treatment strategies.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which intervention is most specifically associated with restoring colonization resistance and treating recurrent Clostridium difficile infections by directly re-establishing a balanced gut microbial community?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Administration of sodium phenylbutyrate   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Prolonged use of broad-spectrum antibiotics   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Implementation of fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT)   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Use of nanoparticle-based drug delivery systems   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Consumption of short-chain fatty acid supplements   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Introduction of indole-producing bacteria   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Increase in dietary fiber intake alone
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
