[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Wait, actually, the bandgap of anatase is about 3.2 eV, which is higher than the energy of visible light (around 2 eV). So pure anatase doesn't absorb visible light effectively. When doped with a transition metal like copper, it might create a lower bandgap, allowing absorption into the visible region. So the bandgap would decrease, not increase. So option 2, which says an increase to 3.6 eV, might not be correct. That would actually make the bandgap higher, requiring higher energy (UV) to excite, which wouldn't help visible light photocatalysis. So probably option 2 is incorrect.
