[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Lactic acid bacteria (LAB) are widely used as probiotics, but their antibiotic resistance profiles must be carefully assessed due to the risk of transferring resistance genes to pathogenic bacteria. Evaluating their susceptibility to various antibiotics and other functional traits is essential for ensuring their safety and efficacy.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which finding most strongly suggests that a specific LAB strain may be a safer probiotic candidate compared to others in terms of antibiotic resistance risk?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) The strain exhibits 100% resistance to oxacillin.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) The strain demonstrates high tolerance to simulated gastric juice (pH 2.0).   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) The strain has a multiple antibiotic resistance (MAR) index below 0.2.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) The strain ferments a broad range of carbohydrates on the API 50 CHL system.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) The strain shows full susceptibility to penicillin.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) The strain is identified to species level using 16S rRNA gene sequencing.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) The strain is isolated from the crop rather than the intestine.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
