[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Enhanced biological phosphorus removal (EBPR) in wastewater treatment relies on specialized bacteria capable of cycling phosphate and carbon under alternating anaerobic and aerobic conditions. Two major bacterial groups, often called polyphosphate-accumulating organisms (PAOs), play distinct roles based on their metabolic capabilities.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following statements correctly distinguishes the metabolic traits of Tetrasphaera from those of Accumulibacter in EBPR systems?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Tetrasphaera stores polyhydroxyalkanoates (PHA) anaerobically, whereas Accumulibacter cannot ferment glucose.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Tetrasphaera can ferment glucose but does not store PHA, whereas Accumulibacter stores PHA but does not ferment glucose.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Both Tetrasphaera and Accumulibacter store PHA anaerobically and ferment glucose.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Accumulibacter stores glycogen aerobically, while Tetrasphaera stores glycogen anaerobically.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Tetrasphaera accumulates polyphosphate only under aerobic conditions, while Accumulibacter does so under anaerobic conditions.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Accumulibacter and Tetrasphaera both require only aerobic conditions for phosphate uptake and storage.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Accumulibacter can ferment glucose and store PHA, while Tetrasphaera performs neither process.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So if the correct answer is 2, then \boxed{2}.
