[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Natural compounds and traditional Chinese medicines (TCM) can modulate the gut microbiota, influence immune responses, and impact cancer progression through diverse mechanisms. These agents may work by altering microbial composition, enhancing beneficial bacteria, strengthening the intestinal barrier, and regulating key inflammatory pathways.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which natural compound or TCM formula is specifically associated with increasing butyrate-producing bacteria and altering the Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes ratio, potentially exerting anticancer effects through these microbiome changes?
