[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Akkermansia muciniphila is a gut bacterium gaining attention for its potential benefits in metabolic and inflammatory diseases. Its unique ability to degrade mucin and modulate host metabolism distinguishes it from many other members of the human microbiota.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following interventions has been shown to significantly increase Akkermansia muciniphila abundance in humans?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) High-protein ketogenic diet   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Probiotic supplementation with Lactobacillus rhamnosus   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Metformin administration   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Antibiotic therapy targeting Gram-negative bacteria   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Omega-3 fatty acid supplementation   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Physical exercise alone   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Fecal microbiota transplantation from obese donors
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
