[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Computational metabolic modeling has become an essential tool for investigating the interactions, metabolic outputs, and community dynamics of gut microbiota in various health and disease states. These approaches integrate genome-scale models to simulate nutrient exchanges and predict the consequences of dietary changes and therapeutic interventions.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following correctly describes a feature or application of multispecies metabolic modeling in gut microbiome research?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) It ignores interactions among microbial species, focusing solely on individual metabolic pathways.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) It relies exclusively on genetic sequencing data, without incorporating metabolomics for validation.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) It enables simulation of metabolic exchanges between multiple microbial species within a shared environment.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) It is restricted to modeling only non-pathogenic microbial communities.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) It cannot predict the cooperative production of metabolites such as butyrate or secondary bile acids.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) It uses only single-organism models, precluding the study of community biomass dynamics.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) It excludes the quantification of metabolic competition or complementarity between microbial pairs.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So, the final answer is \boxed{3}.
