[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Molecular biology research frequently integrates transcriptomic and proteomic techniques to analyze gene and protein expression in bacterial systems. Accurate workflows rely on specialized reagents, instrumentation, and bioinformatics tools to ensure data reliability and experimental reproducibility.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which combination of procedures and reagents would ensure both accurate quantification of bacterial RNA transcripts and downstream validation of protein-protein interactions in Mycobacterium smegmatis?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) RNA extraction with TRIzol and bead beating, qRT-PCR using SuperScript III and DyNAmo SYBR Green kit, yeast two-hybrid assay with LexA-based vectors   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) RNA extraction with NP-40 buffer, DNA removal by bead beating, microarray clustering with anti-HA agarose beads   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Protein extraction using DyNAmo SYBR Green kit, DNA removal with TURBO DNA-free kit, transcript quantification by western blot   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Immunoprecipitation with TRIzol, RNA quantification via yeast two-hybrid assay, gene annotation from GenePix   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Microarray normalization in Partek Genomics Suite, cDNA synthesis with anti-HA agarose beads, protein detection by qRT-PCR   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) RNA extraction using TRIzol, cDNA synthesis with LexA fusion constructs, hierarchical clustering using SuperScript III   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Bead beating for protein extraction, microarray analysis with DyNAmo SYBR Green, protein-protein interaction tested by TURBO DNA-free kit
