[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Psychrophilic and halotolerant bacteria often exhibit unique physiological and genomic adaptations that enable survival in environments with extreme cold and salinity. Understanding these adaptations provides insights into cellular mechanisms for stress resistance.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which feature most strongly suggests that Planococcus halocryophilus Or1 possesses high genomic plasticity, potentially facilitating rapid adaptation to fluctuating environments?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) High abundance of genes involved in amino acid metabolism and transport   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Presence of chaperone and shock protein genes   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Abundance of genes related to unknown or general functions   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Existence of multiple insertion sequences (transposases) from diverse families   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Summed feature 4 in fatty acid analysis   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Nodular and crust-like structures observed by microscopy   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Specialized DEAD-box helicases for low-temperature replication
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
