[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Option 1 says DNA replication and cell division are solely triggered by light intensity. But I remember that Prochlorococcus has an internal timing mechanism, not just relying on light intensity alone. So probably this isn't correct.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Option 2 suggests continuous division without synchronization. But they likely have some synchronization, maybe through the light cycle. Probably not correct.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
