[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m In clinical mycology, accurate identification of black molds is crucial for guiding patient management and public health interventions. Laboratory identification integrates phenotypic features, physiological tests, and optimal culture conditions to distinguish among diverse species and genera.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which combination of diagnostic features and laboratory practices most reliably enables species-level identification of a neurotropic black mold such as Cladophialophora bantiana?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Exclusive use of macroscopic colony color observation on nutrient agar   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Reliance on molecular sequencing without phenotypic evaluation   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Combined assessment of macroscopic and microscopic morphology, supplemented by physiological tests on plant-based media like potato dextrose agar   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Observation of pigment production on blood agar only   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Identification based solely on growth rate at room temperature   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Use of cycloheximide tolerance testing as the sole criterion   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Limiting analysis to genus-level identification using saline wet mount preparations
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So, the final answer is \boxed{3}.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m </think>
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m To accurately identify the neurotropic black mold *Cladophialophora bantiana*, a combination of diagnostic features is necessary. The most reliable approach involves evaluating both macroscopic and microscopic morphology, along with physiological tests using appropriate media like potato dextrose agar. This comprehensive approach ensures species-level identification.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m \boxed{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[RESPONSE][0m ' So, the final answer is \boxed{3}.
