[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Option 6 is a temperature-sensitive plasmid that can replicate at all temperatures. Hmm, temperature-sensitive means that at a certain temperature, the plasmid can't replicate. If the plasmid can't replicate at a certain temp, maybe under selection at that temp, the plasmid can't replicate, forcing integration. But the question is about ensuring only chromosomal gives resistance, so I'm not sure if this is the best approach.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Option 7 is cloning the gene without any antibiotic marker. Wait, then how would they select for the disruption? Without a marker, they wouldn't be able to select for the plasmid or the integration. So probably not the right strategy because you need some way to select for the desired events.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m So, going back, the key is ensuring that the plasmid doesn't replicate, so that the only way the antibiotic resistance is gained is through chromosomal integration. Because if the plasmid can replicate, the resistance could come from the plasmid itself without the gene being integrated.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=1436842)[0m /home/chia/mambaforge/envs/verl/lib/python3.10/site-packages/torch/utils/checkpoint.py:1399: FutureWarning: `torch.cpu.amp.autocast(args...)` is deprecated. Please use `torch.amp.autocast('cpu', args...)` instead.[32m [repeated 7x across cluster][0m
[36m(WorkerDict pid=1436842)[0m   with device_autocast_ctx, torch.cpu.amp.autocast(**cpu_autocast_kwargs), recompute_context:  # type: ignore[attr-defined][32m [repeated 7x across cluster][0m
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m So strategy 2: plasmid lacking an origin recognized by the host. That would mean the plasmid can't replicate, so it would have to integrate into the chromosome to survive. If the origin isn't recognized, the plasmid can't replicate, so it's lost unless it integrates. Therefore, only when the plasmid integrates into the chromosome would the resistance be expressed. Thus, any colonies that survive must have the plasmid integrated into the chromosome, which is the desired event.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m So the correct answer is option 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m </think>
