[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Bacteriophages are viruses that specifically infect bacteria and are being actively researched as alternatives to antibiotics, especially for combating drug-resistant bacterial pathogens. The development and application of phage therapy requires a multidisciplinary approach, integrating genomics, bioinformatics, and an understanding of bacterial defenses.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following is a key advantage of using bioinformatics tools like CGView and Easyfig in the study and therapeutic application of bacteriophages?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) They enable real-time monitoring of phage-induced bacterial cell lysis in clinical samples.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) They facilitate the visualization and comparison of phage genomes to assess genetic diversity and evolutionary relationships.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) They enhance the ability of bacteriophages to evade bacterial defense mechanisms such as CRISPR-Cas.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) They directly increase the infectivity of phage cocktails in treating multi-drug resistant infections.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) They automate the selection of bacterial strains most susceptible to phage infection.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) They produce novel bacteriophage proteins for therapeutic use.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) They prevent the horizontal transfer of virulence factors between bacteria and phages.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So, the correct answer is \boxed{2}.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m </think>
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m The key advantage of using bioinformatics tools like CGView and Easyfig in the study and therapeutic application of bacteriophages is that they facilitate the visualization and comparison of phage genomes to assess genetic diversity and evolutionary relationships. This helps in understanding how phages can be optimized for therapeutic use and how bacterial defenses might evolve against them.
