[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which experimental design element is essential for directly assessing the activity of recombinant Endonuclease III (Nth) in excising oxidatively damaged bases from DNA?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Use of a pQE-30 vector for expressing histidine-tagged proteins in E. coli   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Statistical analysis with one-way ANOVA and Dunnett's test   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Synthesis of an oligonucleotide substrate containing a thymine glycol lesion   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Exposure of bacterial cultures to UV irradiation at 312 nm   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Cloning and sequencing of recombinant protein constructs   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Desalting and storage of purified proteins in defined buffer conditions   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Counting viable cells after incubation post-UV exposure
