[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Lactic acid bacteria such as Oenococcus oeni and Lactobacillus species are essential for malolactic fermentation in winemaking, a process that not only softens wine acidity but also enhances its flavor stability. The adaptation of these bacteria to challenging wine environments involves complex physiological and metabolic responses to stressors like ethanol and acid.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which mechanism specifically aids Oenococcus oeni in maintaining plasma membrane integrity during ethanol stress encountered in winemaking environments?
