[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which experimental condition would most effectively measure the activity of photolyase in bacterial cells following UV-B irradiation?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Incubating cells in complete darkness after UV-B exposure   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Using UV-C light with no visible light during recovery   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Exposing cells to white fluorescent light after UV-B irradiation   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Supplementing cultures with nalidixic acid post-UV treatment   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Adding IPTG to unirradiated cultures without light exposure   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Filtering out UV-B and exposing only to visible light during irradiation   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Increasing lacIq expression during recovery in the dark
