[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Probiotics are increasingly used in poultry production to enhance health and productivity while reducing reliance on antibiotics. Lactic acid bacteria (LAB) are often chosen as probiotics due to their antimicrobial properties and ability to colonize the avian gut.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following characteristics is most critical when selecting lactic acid bacteria strains as host-specific probiotics for poultry to effectively reduce the transmission of zoonotic pathogens?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Ability to ferment a wide variety of carbohydrates   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Tolerance to high salt concentrations in feed   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Production of broad-spectrum antimicrobial compounds active against Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Rapid sporulation under stress conditions   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Resistance to all commonly used antibiotics   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Capability to form biofilms on feed surfaces   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) High rate of genetic mutation for adaptation
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So the final answer is \boxed{3}.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m The question is about selecting lactic acid bacteria (LAB) strains as probiotics for poultry to reduce zoonotic pathogens. The key characteristic is the ability to produce broad-spectrum antimicrobial compounds since this directly targets a wide range of pathogens, including both Gram-positive and Gram-negative, which are common zoonotic threats in poultry.
