[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Enhanced biological phosphorus removal (EBPR) in wastewater treatment relies on the activity of polyphosphate accumulating organisms (PAOs), which vary in their metabolic strategies for phosphorus and carbon cycling. Two important genera, Tetrasphaera and 'Candidatus Accumulibacter phosphatis', exhibit distinct physiological traits that influence their ecological roles in EBPR systems.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which metabolic feature distinguishes Tetrasphaera from 'Candidatus Accumulibacter phosphatis' during the anaerobic phase of EBPR?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Uptake of volatile fatty acids and storage as polyhydroxyalkanoates (PHA)   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Uptake of glucose and fermentation to succinate while synthesizing glycogen   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Use of amino acids as the primary carbon source for phosphorus removal   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Exclusive reliance on nitrate as an electron acceptor under anaerobic conditions   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Inability to perform denitrification   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Direct oxidation of acetate to carbon dioxide for energy storage   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Synthesis of polyhydroxybutyrate as the main energy reserve
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So the final answer is \boxed{2}.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m The correct option is number 2, which states that Tetrasphaera takes up glucose and ferments it to succinate while synthesizing glycogen during the anaerobic phase.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m </think>
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m The correct option is \boxed{2}.
