[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Human cytomegalovirus (HCMV) can infect various human cell types and often interacts with or modulates the host cell's DNA damage response (DDR) pathways. The ability of HCMV to replicate in cells with mutations in key DDR regulators provides insight into its replication strategies and interactions with host defenses.
