[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m The transition from antibiotic use to probiotics in poultry agriculture is driven by concerns over antibiotic resistance and consumer demand for safer food products. Effective probiotic development for poultry requires careful selection and validation of beneficial bacterial strains, often tailored to local conditions and host species.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which approach is most likely to ensure that probiotic products are both effective and well-adapted for poultry production in a particular country such as Bangladesh?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Importing commercially available probiotic products from international manufacturers   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Selecting lactic acid bacteria strains from dairy products used in human foods   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Isolating and characterizing lactic acid bacteria strains from the gastrointestinal tracts of local broiler chickens   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Using genetically modified bacteria engineered for high growth rates   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Relying on generic probiotic blends with undisclosed strain information   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Applying broad-spectrum antibiotics in combination with probiotics   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Supplementing poultry feed with herbal extracts alone
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So, the final answer is \boxed{3}.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m </think>
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
