[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following statements accurately describes Ignavibacterium album in comparison to classical green sulfur bacteria (GSB) within the Chlorobi phylum?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) It is capable of obligate photoautotrophy using reduced sulfur compounds as electron donors.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) It possesses photosynthetic pigments and essential photosynthesis genes.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) It can grow phototrophically under strictly anaerobic conditions.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) It is a metabolically versatile, non-phototrophic bacterium distantly related to green sulfur bacteria.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) It has been shown to oxidize ferrous iron as its primary electron donor.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) It is strictly an obligate anaerobe unable to tolerate oxygen.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) It is the first Chlorobi shown to fix nitrogen under oxic conditions.
