[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Ammonia-oxidizing bacteria (AOB) play a crucial role in the nitrogen cycle by converting ammonia to nitrite, a process that can lead to the emission of greenhouse gases such as nitric oxide (NO) and nitrous oxide (N2O). Understanding the genetic, ecological, and evolutionary factors that influence these emissions is important for managing their environmental impact.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which experimental design element most directly ensures that observed differences in NO and N2O production among AOB strains can be attributed to genetic or physiological variability rather than to differences in cultivation conditions?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Use of multiple strains representing diverse phylogenetic clusters   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Measurement of nitrite (NO2-) concentration to monitor substrate consumption   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Selection of strains with closed genomes for comprehensive gene analysis   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Standardization of temperature, medium, pH, and ammonium concentrations during cultivation   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Conducting microrespirometry at 28°C with late-log phase cells   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Exclusion of strains lacking closed genomes from comparative analyses   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Application of phylogenetic analysis on 400 conserved proteins
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So, the final answer is \boxed{4}.
