[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following statements accurately describes an application or property of a bacterial strain relevant to food or biomedical science?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Lactococcus lactis-derived biosurfactants can inhibit microbial adhesion on silicone rubber surfaces.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Meat-borne Lactobacillus strains universally produce high levels of biogenic amines.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Staphylococcus aureus adhesion to polypropylene surfaces is unaffected by temperature variations.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) All lactobacilli isolated from Portuguese olives lack probiotic potential.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Yogurt containing Bifidobacterium animalis subsp. lactis BB-12 reduces beneficial fecal bacterial counts in healthy adults.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Propionibacterium acnes fermentation is incapable of influencing MRSA colonization on skin.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Enterococci from food sources never harbor antibiotic resistance or virulence factors.
