[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Green sulfur bacteria are anoxygenic phototrophs that play a significant role in sulfur cycling by utilizing light energy and oxidizing reduced sulfur compounds. Advances in sequencing technologies and genetic manipulation have facilitated in-depth studies of their unique metabolic pathways and adaptations.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following best describes the primary process by which green sulfur bacteria obtain energy in anoxic environments?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Oxidation of water using oxygenic photosynthesis   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Fermentation of organic substrates in the absence of light   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Aerobic respiration utilizing molecular oxygen as the terminal electron acceptor   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Oxidation of reduced sulfur compounds coupled to anoxygenic photosynthesis   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Methanogenesis using carbon dioxide as the electron acceptor   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Nitrogen fixation from atmospheric nitrogen   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Reverse electron transport for carbon fixation without light
