[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which feature most reliably distinguishes Rothia dentocariosa from similar genera such as Nocardia, Actinomyces, and Corynebacterium in a clinical microbiology laboratory?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Rapid growth on minimal media with inorganic nitrogen   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Production of diaminopimelic acid and arabinose in the cell wall   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Strict anaerobic metabolism   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Positive acid-fast staining   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Inability to grow on inorganic nitrogen and unique cell wall composition   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Formation of endospores   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Motility in liquid culture
