[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which set of envelope-associated proteins in Gram-negative bacteria directly contributes to both nutrient uptake and antibiotic resistance?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Surface adhesins and secretion system type II components   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Influx and efflux pumps   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Lipoproteins and cytoplasmic chaperones   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Periplasmic chaperones and outer membrane porins   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Secretion system type V components and sugar transporters   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Cytoplasmic chaperones and surface adhesins   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Porins and periplasmic chaperones
