[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following is a primary reason for assigning ‘Candidatus’ status to a bacterium involved in wastewater treatment processes?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Its ability to store polyphosphate under anoxic conditions   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Its slow growth and inability to be fully maintained in pure culture   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Its preference for lipid substrates in activated sludge   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Its high sequence similarity to closely related species   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Its hydrophobic cell surface facilitating substrate uptake   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Its contradictory metabolic behavior in situ and in pure culture   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Its contribution to foaming in wastewater plants
