[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m During periods of nitrogen limitation in lakes with persistent Microcystis blooms, which set of genes is most likely to be upregulated to enhance nitrogen acquisition and utilization?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) psbA, psaB, and petE (photosystem and electron transport proteins)   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) rbcL, cbbX, and prk (Calvin cycle enzymes)   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) ntcA, amt, nrt, ure, and urt (nitrogen regulation and transport)   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) glgA, glgC, and glgP (glycogen metabolism)   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) cysD, cysN, and cysC (sulfur assimilation)   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) mcyA, mcyB, and mcyD (microcystin synthesis)   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) sodA, katG, and prx (oxidative stress response)
