[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Bacteria employ a range of physiological and genetic mechanisms to survive environmental stresses, including nutrient deprivation, oxidative damage, dehydration, salinity, and osmotic pressure. Understanding these adaptations is central to advancing microbial ecology, biotechnology, and agriculture.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following adaptations most directly contributes to bacterial survival during desiccation by stabilizing cellular structures in a glass-like state?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Production of catalase enzymes to degrade hydrogen peroxide   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Synthesis of biofilm polysaccharides for surface attachment   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Accumulation of compatible solutes such as trehalose   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Upregulation of rpoN-dependent nitrogen assimilation genes   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Remodeling of membrane fatty acid composition in response to solutes   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Activation of alternative sigma factors for global gene regulation   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Induction of stationary phase mutagenesis mechanisms
