[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following statements most accurately describes a unique mechanism by which Saccharomyces boulardii contributes to intestinal health in animals and humans?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) It produces lipopeptides that directly lyse the cell walls of Escherichia coli K88.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) It secretes a protease that neutralizes the toxins of Clostridium difficile.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) It acts as a bacteriophage, infecting and lysing Clostridium perfringens directly.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) It generates bacteriocins effective against Salmonella and Listeria exclusively.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) It colonizes the gut to outcompete Lactobacillus fermentum and reduce inflammation.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) It alters the protein content of animal diets to reduce necrotic enteritis risk.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) It synthesizes lantibiotics that inhibit Ruminococcus gnavus growth.
