[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Genome-scale metabolic models (GSMMs) are essential tools for understanding and engineering microbial metabolism. Accurately representing cellular growth and energetics in these models requires careful integration of physiological data, metabolic constraints, and energy maintenance parameters.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m In constructing a GSMM for a yeast strain used in recombinant protein production, which methodological approach best ensures that the energy costs of macromolecule polymerization are accurately accounted for without double-counting, while maintaining realistic growth predictions?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Including polymerization energy directly in the biomass equation and omitting it from all maintenance parameters   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Excluding polymerization energy from the biomass equation and incorporating it solely in the non-growth associated maintenance (NGAM) term   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Distributing polymerization energy equally between the biomass equation and both NGAM and GAM parameters   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Representing polymerization energy exclusively within the growth associated maintenance (GAM) parameter, while omitting it from the biomass equation   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Modeling polymerization energy as a separate reversible reaction unconstrained by growth rate data   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Assigning polymerization energy to be proportional to the flux of all exchange reactions   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Ignoring polymerization energy costs entirely to simplify the model
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So the final answer is \boxed{2}.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
