[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which diagnostic advancement most directly addresses the challenge of differentiating Nocardia infections from those caused by mycobacteria due to antigenic cross-reactivity?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Use of metabolic profiling for oxidative versus fermentative metabolism   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Development of monoclonal antibody-based serological assays   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Antimicrobial susceptibility testing using extended incubation periods   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Observation of colony morphology and aerial mycelium formation   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Staining for acid-fast cell wall properties   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Cultivation on selective media containing antibiotics   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Measurement of arylsulfatase enzyme activity
