[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Real-time PCR assays, such as LC-PCR, are crucial tools in detecting and quantifying low levels of pathogenic bacteria like Mycobacterium avium subsp. paratuberculosis (MAP) in complex samples such as milk. The sensitivity and accuracy of these assays depend heavily on both DNA extraction protocols and the ability to overcome PCR inhibitors present in the sample matrix.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m When optimizing a protocol for sensitive detection of MAP in raw milk using LC-PCR, which combination of DNA extraction steps most effectively improves both cell lysis and removal of inhibitors, thereby enhancing detection sensitivity?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Heat lysis followed by simple ethanol precipitation   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Bead-beating alone without enzymatic treatment   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Proteinase K treatment followed by phenol-chloroform extraction   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Use of a nucleic acid binding column without prior cell disruption   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Ribolysis combined with proteinase K treatment and column-based purification   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Direct PCR on untreated milk samples   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Alkaline lysis with isopropanol precipitation
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So the final answer is \boxed{5}.
