[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Melanized fungi, also called dematiaceous or black fungi, are a diverse group of pathogens characterized by dark pigmentation arising from melanin in their cell walls. These organisms can cause a spectrum of human diseases, particularly in immunocompromised individuals, and present unique diagnostic and therapeutic challenges.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following is the principal reason melanin is considered a key virulence factor in melanized fungi?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) It accelerates fungal growth rates in nutrient-poor environments.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) It facilitates adhesion of fungi to host epithelial cells.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) It provides resistance to oxidative stress and host immune defenses.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) It enhances antifungal drug uptake, improving treatment outcomes.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) It enables the secretion of proteolytic enzymes for tissue invasion.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) It disrupts normal host cell signaling pathways.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) It increases susceptibility of fungi to phagocytosis by immune cells.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So the final answer is just \boxed{3}.
