[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Advances in nanomedicine have led to the development of multifunctional nanosystems designed to target multidrug-resistant bacterial infections, such as those caused by MRSA. These systems often combine targeted drug delivery, immune evasion, real-time imaging, and responsive release mechanisms.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which feature of a selenium-based nanosystem coated with red blood cell membrane most directly enables it to circulate longer in the bloodstream and evade immune system clearance?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Fluorescence imaging capability of Ru-Se nanoparticles   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Degradation of gelatin nanoparticles by bacterial enzymes   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Antimicrobial properties of selenium nanoparticles   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Functionalization with a ruthenium complex   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Biomimetic camouflage provided by red blood cell membrane coating   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Enhanced wound healing due to rapid bacterial elimination   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Triggered release of nanoparticles at infection sites
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So the final answer is just a number, like \boxed{5}.
