[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Looking back at the question, it asks which property is characteristic of outer membrane proteins in Gram-negative bacteria, crucial for nutrient uptake and host interaction.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m The options are:
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) α-helical transmembrane domains – inner membranes might have this, but outer? Not sure.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Exclusively inner membrane – outer membrane proteins shouldn't be here.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) β-barrel structure in outer membrane. I remember that outer membrane proteins often have beta barrel structures, like porins.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m So the correct answer is option 3, which is \boxed{3}.
