[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m LapD binds c-di-GMP. So if c-di-GMP decreases, LapD doesn't bind, so LapG is active.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m LapG activity: if LapG is active, it would cleave LapA. So if LapG is active, LapA is cleaved and released, leading to dispersal.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m So the sequence would be: phosphate starvation causes c-di-GMP levels to decrease. Lower c-di-GMP means RapA is repressed? Or does higher c-di-GMP lead to higher RapA? Or is it the opposite? I'm a bit confused.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
