[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Bacteriophages are increasingly explored as alternatives to antibiotics for treating infections caused by antibiotic-resistant bacteria, such as Enterococcus faecalis, especially in dental and hospital settings. Certain phage characteristics, including host range, burst size, latency, and environmental stability, are critical for therapeutic effectiveness.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which feature most distinguishes the lytic phage HEf13 from previously described E. faecalis phages in terms of its suitability for treating dental infections?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Limited ability to infect non-oral E. faecalis strains   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Host range restricted to less than 10% of tested isolates   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Sensitivity to temperatures above 30°C   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) High burst size and broad host range among dental clinical isolates   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Prolonged latent period exceeding 50 minutes   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Instability at acidic and alkaline pH values   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Ineffectiveness at low multiplicity of infection (MOI) levels
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So the final answer is just a single number, like \boxed{4}.
