[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Probiotics and beneficial bacteria are increasingly used in food safety, agriculture, and health for their ability to inhibit pathogens and promote a balanced microbiome. Understanding the mechanisms by which these microorganisms exert their effects is essential for developing effective applications.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which property is most critical for a lactic acid bacterium to successfully colonize a mucosal surface and competitively exclude pathogens in the gastrointestinal tract?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Production of heat-stable hemolysins   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Ability to adhere to and aggregate on mucosal surfaces   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Resistance to all antibiotics   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Production of biocides in large quantities   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Complete inability to form biofilms   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=1436842)[0m /home/chia/mambaforge/envs/verl/lib/python3.10/site-packages/torch/utils/checkpoint.py:1399: FutureWarning: `torch.cpu.amp.autocast(args...)` is deprecated. Please use `torch.amp.autocast('cpu', args...)` instead.[32m [repeated 7x across cluster][0m
