[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Actinomycetes comprise a diverse group of gram-positive bacteria, some of which are clinically significant as opportunistic pathogens, particularly in immunocompromised individuals. Advances in bacterial taxonomy and antibiotic resistance have implications for accurate diagnosis and effective treatment.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following statements best characterizes the clinical and microbiological features of Rothia and its antibiotic susceptibility profile?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Rothia species are uniformly identified by serologic tests and are highly susceptible to clindamycin.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) All Rothia strains are resistant to penicillin but susceptible to beta-lactam antibiotics.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Rothia infections are typically treated with penicillin, but some strains may exhibit resistance to beta-lactam antibiotics.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Rothia dentocariosa cannot cause disease in animal models and is non-pathogenic.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Most Rothia strains are highly resistant to all antibiotics, including lincomycin.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Rothia species are gram-negative rods with uniform biochemical characteristics.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Rothia species are exclusively found in soil and never cause human infections.
