[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Pseudomonas aeruginosa relies on robust genetic systems to survive oxidative stress and DNA damage, with multiple regulatory factors mediating these defenses. The OxyR transcription factor and its associated genes play a central role in orchestrating antioxidant responses.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following most accurately describes a key reason why deletion of the oxyR gene in Pseudomonas aeruginosa leads to heightened sensitivity to oxidative stress that cannot be fully rescued by restoring a single downstream antioxidant enzyme?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) OxyR regulates multiple genes involved in oxidative stress, creating a multifaceted defense network.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) OxyR directly catalyzes the breakdown of hydrogen peroxide independent of gene regulation.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) The absence of OxyR leads to overproduction of iron, eliminating cellular antioxidant capacity.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Only one antioxidant enzyme in the OxyR regulon is essential for survival under oxidative stress.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Deletion of oxyR disrupts a unique small RNA found in P. aeruginosa responsible for stress responses.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) OxyR exclusively influences DNA repair enzymes, not antioxidant enzymes.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) OxyR is only activated in high-iron environments and is inactive otherwise.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So the final answer is just a single number between \boxed{} tags.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
