[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m In food processing environments, biofilms formed by microbial communities contribute to persistent contamination and food spoilage. Plant-derived essential oils are studied for their potential to inhibit biofilm formation and exhibit antioxidant activity.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which statement most accurately describes a mechanism by which essential oils inhibit biofilm-related contamination in food processing environments?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Essential oils disrupt bacterial quorum sensing, preventing coordinated biofilm formation.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Essential oils increase reactive oxygen species production, accelerating biofilm growth.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Essential oils enhance the adhesive abilities of bacteria on plastic and metal surfaces.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Essential oils promote the synthesis of polysaccharides in the biofilm matrix.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Essential oils induce DNA repair systems that strengthen mature biofilms.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Essential oils neutralize antimicrobial cleaning agents, reducing overall efficacy.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Essential oils selectively stimulate pathogenic bacteria over spoilage organisms.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
