[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following statements most accurately describes the relationship between heavy metal resistance and antibiotic resistance observed in bacteria isolated from sewage treatment environments?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) All bacteria resistant to heavy metals are also highly susceptible to antibiotics.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) The majority of heavy metal-resistant bacteria isolated exhibit resistance to multiple antibiotics.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) No correlation exists between heavy metal resistance and antibiotic resistance in environmental bacteria.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Only Gram-positive bacteria show heavy metal and antibiotic resistance simultaneously.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Bacteria resistant to heavy metals are generally unable to tolerate mixtures of metals.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) All isolates showed resistance exclusively to nickel, the least tolerated metal.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Heavy metal-resistant bacteria are always non-pathogenic and pose no health risk.
