[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Fungal infections of the central nervous system (CNS) and respiratory tract can be caused by a diverse range of opportunistic and environmental molds, posing diagnostic and therapeutic challenges, particularly in immunocompromised patients. Some fungi possess unique pathogenic features, such as melanin production, contributing to their virulence and resistance to treatment.
