[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Option 3 says MRN complex phosphorylates Mre11 and 53BP1 is phosphorylated. Not sure about that. I think MRN is more about ATM activation, maybe.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Option 1 says ATM activation drives γH2AX, and 53BP1 remains stable. But if the stress is more replication-related (so ATR), then γH2AX might be due to ATR, not just ATM.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Option 5 says both ATM and ATR equally, which doesn't seem right. So option 2 seems better.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Therefore, the correct answer is option 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m </think>
