[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which statement most accurately describes the limitations of using 16S rRNA gene sequencing as a primary tool for microbiome analysis in modeling recovery after perturbation?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) It provides comprehensive functional information about all microbial genes.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) It reliably identifies non-bacterial community members such as fungi and viruses.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) It is more expensive and less accessible than shotgun metagenomics.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) It lacks the capacity to detect functional metabolic pathways within the microbiome.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) It can quantify microbial stability but not diversity.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) It automatically distinguishes between healthy and unhealthy microbiomes.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) It enables precise identification of strain-level genetic variation across all microbes.
