[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m In microbial transcriptomics, high-throughput sequencing and advanced bioinformatics tools are used to analyze gene expression under various environmental conditions. This workflow is especially valuable for studying extremophiles, such as psychrophilic bacteria, that thrive in cold environments and exhibit unique physiological adaptations.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following sequences correctly outlines the main steps used for transcriptomic analysis of gene expression in a psychrophilic bacterium exposed to cold and osmotic stress?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) DNA extraction → whole genome amplification → Illumina sequencing → Bowtie2 alignment → FastQC → DESeq analysis   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) RNA extraction → cDNA synthesis → RNase H treatment → GenomiPHI V2 amplification → Illumina Hi-Seq 2000 sequencing → FastQC/PRINSEQ → Bowtie2 alignment → htseq-count quantification → DESeq analysis   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Protein extraction → Western blotting → mass spectrometry → heat map generation   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) RNA extraction → cDNA synthesis → direct Sanger sequencing → DESeq analysis   
