[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Tsukamurella paurometabola is a psychrophilic actinomycete occasionally implicated in human disease, while environmental actinomycetes are more commonly associated with hypersensitivity reactions rather than true infections. Accurate laboratory differentiation is important due to the clinical implications of both contamination and infection.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which characteristic most reliably differentiates Tsukamurella paurometabola from thermophilic actinomycetes when identifying a clinical isolate?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Ability to thrive at high temperatures   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Predominant association with hypersensitivity pneumonitis   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Presence of distinctive mycolic acid profiles in the cell wall   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Frequent isolation from immunocompetent patients   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Gram-negative staining reaction   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Susceptibility to amoxicillin-clavulanate   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Isolation primarily from organic dusts
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So the final answer is just a single boxed number between the tags.
