[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Mono-ADP-ribosyltransferases (ARTs) and poly-ADP-ribosyl polymerases (PARPs) are enzymes that mediate ADP-ribosylation, an important regulatory post-translational modification found in both prokaryotes and eukaryotes. The enzyme Arr, a mono-ADP-ribosyltransferase present in certain mycobacteria, is associated with antibiotic resistance and potentially with cellular responses to DNA damage.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which statement accurately describes a unique property of the Arr enzyme in Mycobacterium smegmatis that distinguishes it from many other well-studied prokaryotic ARTs?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Arr is a secreted toxin that modifies host cell proteins during infection.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Arr is involved in the poly-ADP-ribosylation of bacterial DNA repair proteins.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Arr confers resistance to rifampin by ADP-ribosylating and inactivating the antibiotic molecule.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Arr is exclusively found in eukaryotic and archaebacterial species.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Arr modifies host immune responses through extracellular secretion.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Arr builds long chains of ADP-ribose on target proteins like eukaryotic PARPs.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Arr is responsible for recruiting DNA polymerases to DSBs by direct binding.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So the final answer is just a single boxed number between the tags.
