[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Harmful algal blooms caused by cyanobacteria, such as Microcystis aeruginosa, threaten freshwater systems and public health due to their production of microcystin toxins. Effective management of these blooms requires understanding the ecological drivers and implementing appropriate mitigation strategies.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following approaches is recognized as most effective for controlling toxic cyanobacterial blooms in large, shallow, eutrophic lakes?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Reducing only phosphorus inputs from agricultural runoff   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Enhancing aeration to increase water mixing   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Applying algaecides during peak bloom periods   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Implementing dual nutrient management by reducing both nitrogen and phosphorus inputs   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Increasing fish stocking to alter food web dynamics   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Introducing competitive non-toxic algae species   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Relying solely on advanced toxin detection methods in water treatment plants
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So the final answer is just a single boxed number between the tags.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Looking at the options, I remember that controlling both nitrogen and phosphorus is more effective than just one. So looking at options 1 and 4: option 1 only reduces phosphorus, while option 4 reduces both. I think option 4 is better.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m So the correct answer is \boxed{4}.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m </think>
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m \boxed{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[RESPONSE][0m ' So the final answer is just a single boxed number between the tags.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Looking at the options, I remember that controlling both nitrogen and phosphorus is more effective than just one. So looking at options 1 and 4: option 1 only reduces phosphorus, while option 4 reduces both. I think option 4 is better.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m So the correct answer is \boxed{4}.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m </think>
