[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Aerobic actinomycetes, particularly those in the genus Nocardia, pose significant diagnostic and therapeutic challenges due to their variable clinical presentations and complex taxonomy. Accurate species identification is crucial for effective management and understanding of their epidemiology.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following advances has most significantly improved the accurate classification of Nocardia species and reduced previous misclassification with related bacteria?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Routine Gram staining and colony morphology assessment   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Basic carbohydrate fermentation testing   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Acid-fast staining techniques alone   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Chemotaxonomic analysis of cell wall components and DNA studies   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Use of broad-spectrum antibiotics in therapy trials   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Clinical symptom comparison across patient populations   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Serological testing for Nocardia-specific antibodies
