[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which technique is primarily used in quantitative proteomics to compare protein abundance across different samples by incorporating distinct stable isotopic labels into proteins?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Two-dimensional electrophoresis   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Western blotting   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Stable isotope labeling   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) HMMER sequence analysis   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) VirulentPred prediction   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Polymerase chain reaction (PCR)   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Blast2GO annotation
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
