[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Oenococcus oeni is a lactic acid bacterium crucial for malolactic fermentation in winemaking, where it must adapt to challenging conditions such as high ethanol, low pH, and limited nutrients. Understanding its metabolic pathways and stress responses is key for controlling fermentation quality and product characteristics.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following metabolic pathways in Oenococcus oeni is primarily responsible for the conversion of malic acid to lactic acid during malolactic fermentation, thereby reducing wine acidity?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Heterolactic fermentation pathway   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Citrate degradation pathway   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Glycolytic (Embden-Meyerhof-Parnas) pathway   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Malolactic enzyme pathway   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Mannitol fermentation pathway   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Acetoin biosynthesis pathway   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Ethanol fermentation pathway
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
