[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which combination of analysis tools and statistical methods is best suited for (1) aligning sequencing reads to detect antibiotic resistance genes, (2) visualizing community structure differences, and (3) testing for functional differences between groups, while controlling for multiple hypothesis testing?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Bowtie2 for gene alignment, Principal Component Analysis for community visualization, t-test without correction for group comparisons   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) DIAMOND for gene alignment, NMDS based on Bray-Curtis dissimilarity for community visualization, Wilcoxon rank-sum test with Storey’s adjustment for group comparisons   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) BWA-MEM for gene alignment, UPGMA clustering for community visualization, ANOVA for group comparisons with Bonferroni correction   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) BLASTn for gene alignment, PCoA based on Jaccard distance for community visualization, Kruskal-Wallis test without adjustment   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) DIAMOND for gene alignment, hierarchical clustering for community visualization, Mann-Whitney U test with Holm correction   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) BWA for gene alignment, t-SNE for community visualization, Fisher’s exact test with Benjamini-Hochberg correction   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) BLAT for gene alignment, DCA ordination for community visualization, Student’s t-test with no multiple testing correction
