[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Dematiaceous (melanized) fungi are environmental molds known for their dark pigmentation and ability to cause a variety of human diseases, ranging from allergies to invasive infections. Understanding the clinical manifestations and management of allergic responses to these fungi is important in respiratory and sinonasal medicine.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following findings is most characteristic of allergic fungal sinusitis (AFS) caused by dematiaceous fungi in immunocompetent individuals?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Invasive growth of fungal hyphae into sinus tissues   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Frequent response to standard antibiotic therapy alone   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Presence of nasal polyps and allergic mucin without tissue invasion   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) High prevalence of Alternaria-specific IgG in all patients   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Exclusive causation by Aspergillus species   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Lack of radiographic abnormalities on CT scan   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Predominant occurrence in immunocompromised individuals
