[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Nanomaterials such as zinc oxide nanoparticles (ZnONPs) and carbon nanotubes (CNTs) are widely used in cosmetics, medicine, and the food industry for their unique physical, chemical, and antimicrobial properties. However, concerns remain regarding their safety, cytotoxicity, and effects on human microbiota.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which characteristic of carbon nanotubes (CNTs) most directly determines whether their antibacterial action proceeds predominantly by piercing bacterial membranes or by wrapping around bacterial cells?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Electrical conductivity of CNTs   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Length of CNTs   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Biodegradability of CNTs   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Surface charge of CNTs   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Diameter of CNTs   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Chemical composition of CNTs   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Aggregation state of CNTs
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
