[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Preventing necrotic enteritis (NE) in poultry is crucial for maintaining flock health and productivity, especially as the use of antibiotic growth promoters decreases due to regulatory and consumer pressures. Strategies involving gut microbiota management, such as competitive exclusion cultures, probiotics, and prebiotics, have been explored to control NE and improve performance.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which intervention strategy has been shown to provide the greatest reduction in NE-associated mortality, gut lesions, and pathogen load in broiler chickens?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Administration of single-strain probiotics alone   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Feeding an NE-predisposing high-protein diet without additives   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Use of antibiotics exclusively from day one   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Early administration of prebiotics alone, such as MOS   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Combined use of competitive exclusion cultures, probiotics, and prebiotics   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Supplementation with yeast extract only during the first 10 days   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Inclusion of Lactobacillus acidophilus as the sole beneficial bacteria
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So the final answer is just \boxed{5}.
