[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which feature most directly enables Lactobacillus reuteri to survive the toxic effects of bile salts in the intestine and also influences host cholesterol metabolism?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Production of exopolysaccharides   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Expression of the MapA surface protein   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Bile salt hydrolase activity   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Acid tolerance response   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Induction of mucin gene expression   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Free radical scavenging enzymes   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) S-layer protein formation
