[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Melanized (dematiaceous) fungi are a diverse group of molds that produce melanin in their cell walls, contributing to their resistance against environmental stresses and immune defenses. Understanding the biosynthetic pathways and the role of melanin is critical for appreciating their pathogenic mechanisms and clinical significance.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which characteristic most specifically distinguishes the melanin biosynthesis pathway of dematiaceous fungi from that of other pathogenic fungi such as Cryptococcus neoformans?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Utilization of L-DOPA as the melanin precursor   
