[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m [34mℹ[0m [1m[34m[QUESTION][0m Photocatalytic antimicrobial coatings are increasingly explored to curb microbial contamination on indoor surfaces, particularly where moisture promotes pathogen survival. Titanium dioxide (TiO2) is a common base for such coatings, but its activity is limited to UV light unless modified.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Which of the following most directly explains how copper doping enhances the antimicrobial efficacy of TiO2 coatings under visible light illumination?
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 1) Copper increases the coating's hydrophobicity, preventing biofilm formation.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 2) Copper narrows the TiO2 band gap, enabling absorption of visible light and promoting reactive oxygen species generation.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 3) Copper acts as an independent antibacterial agent, releasing ions that kill microbes in darkness.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 4) Copper improves the mechanical durability of the coating, allowing longer service life.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 5) Copper enhances the adhesion of TiO2 particles to surfaces, reducing contamination risk.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 6) Copper increases the porosity of the TiO2 layer, facilitating microbial entrapment.   
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 7) Copper suppresses the formation of the rutile phase, which is less active photocatalytically.
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1434988)[0m Please provide your reasoning within <think></think> tags and the final answer within a \boxed{} block. The value inside the \boxed{} block should only be the number of the correct option. So the final answer is just \boxed{2}.
